.TH CHIMERACTL 1 "September 2026" "Chimera Spawn 1.0.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
chimeractl \- administer a Chimera Spawn server
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B chimeractl
[\fICOMMAND\fR] [\fIOPTIONS\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B chimeractl
is the administrative client for Chimera Spawn. It talks to
.B chimera-server
over a local Unix-domain HTTP/WebSocket socket authenticated with
.BR SO_PEERCRED ,
or over HTTPS/WSS with mandatory mutual TLS when
.B \-\-host
is set.
.PP
Members of
.B chimera-admin
can operate an installed local server without
.BR sudo
after a fresh login session. An explicit
.B \-\-socket
selects a non-default local server socket.
.PP
.B exec
runs a command inside a managed container with
.B systemd-run --machine --wait --pty|--pipe --collect --service-type=exec --expand-environment=no
and a unique
.B chimera-exec-<id>.service
unit. The CLI returns the guest exit status. Disconnect or server shutdown
stops that exact unit. Command arguments are not placed in the WebSocket URL.
A TTY session forwards the client's
.B TERM
as stream-start metadata and applies it with
.BR --setenv=TERM=... .
Redirected sessions do not invent a terminal type, and the client does not
forward arbitrary process environment.
.B shell
uses
.BR "machinectl shell"
and does not propagate a guest status.
.PP
.B spawn
is a deprecated alias for
.BR launch .
Create and launch default to catalog profile
.B standard
when
.B \-\-profile
is omitted.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B create IMAGE NAME
Create a stopped container.
.TP
.B launch IMAGE NAME
Create and start a container.
.TP
.B spawn IMAGE NAME
Deprecated alias for launch. It accepts the same workload options.
.TP
.B logs NAME
Stream the managed container's guest journal from the server host. Use
.B \-\-supervisor
for the host-side
.B systemd-nspawn@NAME.service
journal.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-s ", " \-\-socket =\fIPATH\fR
Local Unix socket. Mutually exclusive with
.BR \-\-host .
Command-local; there is no top-level socket flag.
.TP
.BR \-H ", " \-\-host =\fIHOST[:PORT]\fR
Remote server. Always HTTPS/WSS. Default port 8080.
.TP
.B \-\-tls-ca \fIPATH\fR
Trust anchor for the remote server certificate.
.TP
.B \-\-tls-cert \fIPATH\fR
Client certificate. Root-equivalent remote administration.
.TP
.B \-\-tls-key \fIPATH\fR
Client private key.
.TP
.B \-\-format \fItable|json\fR
Output format. JSON is machine-readable on stdout.
.TP
.B \-\-timeout \fISECONDS\fR
HTTP setup and WebSocket handshake timeout. It does not abort a started guest command.
.SS Create, launch, and spawn workload options
.TP
.B \-\-bind \fISOURCE:DEST[:OPTIONS]\fR
Add a writable native nspawn bind mount. Repeatable.
.TP
.B \-\-bind-ro \fISOURCE:DEST[:OPTIONS]\fR
Add a read-only native nspawn bind mount. Repeatable. Escape literal path colons as
.BR \e: .
.TP
.B \-\-tmpfs \fIDEST[:OPTIONS]\fR
Add a native nspawn temporary filesystem. Repeatable.
.TP
.B \-\-publish \fISPEC\fR
Publish a port. Accepted forms are PORT, HOST:CONTAINER,
tcp:HOST:CONTAINER, and udp:HOST:CONTAINER. Repeatable.
.TP
.B \-\-memory-high \fISIZE\fR
Set systemd MemoryHigh for this container.
.TP
.B \-\-memory-max \fISIZE\fR
Set systemd MemoryMax for this container.
.TP
.B \-\-memory-swap-max \fISIZE\fR
Set systemd MemorySwapMax for this container.
.TP
.B \-\-tasks-max \fIN\fR
Set a positive systemd TasksMax.
.TP
.B \-\-cpu-quota \fIPERCENT\fR
Set a positive CPUQuota percentage; 600 renders as 600%.
.TP
.B \-\-cpu-weight \fIN\fR
Set CPUWeight in the range 1 through 10000.
.TP
.B \-\-io-weight \fIN\fR
Set IOWeight in the range 1 through 10000.
.SS Logs options
.TP
.BR \-u ", " \-\-unit \fIUNIT\fR
Select a guest journal unit.
.TP
.BR \-n ", " \-\-lines \fIN\fR
Show N initial records. Default 200.
.TP
.BR \-f ", " \-\-follow
Follow new records until interrupted.
.TP
.B \-\-supervisor
Read the host nspawn service journal. This may be used while the machine is stopped
and cannot be combined with
.BR \-\-unit .
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /run/chimera-spawn/server.sock
Default installed Unix socket.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR chimera-server (1)
.PP
